 "cues": [
  {
   "text": "A lot of AI agents and orchestration platforms",
   "start": 2.5,
   "end": 5.184
  },
  {
   "text": "today do their job by asking a big,",
   "start": 5.184,
   "end": 7.338
  },
  {
   "text": "slow language model a question at every step.",
   "start": 7.338,
   "end": 10.107
  },
  {
   "text": "Dreaming learns to answer the repetitive",
   "start": 10.107,
   "end": 11.782
  },
  {
   "text": "questions in milliseconds for almost nothing,",
   "start": 11.782,
   "end": 14.432
  },
  {
   "text": "and this really matters for a lot",
   "start": 14.432,
   "end": 15.731
  },
  {
   "text": "of companies that are running expensive",
   "start": 15.731,
   "end": 17.372
  },
  {
   "text": "workflows almost thousands of times a day.",
   "start": 17.372,
   "end": 19.731
  },
  {
   "text": "We can slash those costs by up to 87%",
   "start": 19.731,
   "end": 22.226
  },
  {
   "text": "while lowering processing latency",
   "start": 22.226,
   "end": 23.97
  },
  {
   "text": "from 2.6 seconds to 5 milliseconds using",
   "start": 23.97,
   "end": 27.269
  },
  {
   "text": "our novel workflow language model, Psi.",
   "start": 27.269,
   "end": 29.808
  },
  {
   "text": "So let's start by running 2,000 workflow runs.",
   "start": 29.808,
   "end": 32.473
  },
  {
   "text": "What's amazing about Psi is that it can pick",
   "start": 32.473,
   "end": 34.267
  },
  {
   "text": "up on workflow results quickly and with little",
   "start": 34.267,
   "end": 36.49
  },
  {
   "text": "data with its structural memory capabilities.",
   "start": 36.49,
   "end": 39.225
  },
  {
   "text": "Of course, a lot of companies have different error",
   "start": 39.225,
   "end": 41.242
  },
  {
   "text": "rates depending on how strong they want their models",
   "start": 41.242,
   "end": 43.259
  },
  {
   "text": "to be. For ours, we compute a statistical",
   "start": 43.259,
   "end": 45.84
  },
  {
   "text": "bound on the error and we only allow our stand-ins",
   "start": 45.84,
   "end": 48.421
  },
  {
   "text": "to take over when that bound is under your budget.",
   "start": 48.421,
   "end": 50.91
  },
  {
   "text": "You can adjust that by clicking on the Dreams tab",
   "start": 50.91,
   "end": 52.927
  },
  {
   "text": "here and adjusting the number of allowed mistakes",
   "start": 52.927,
   "end": 55.047
  },
  {
   "text": "and watching coverage shrink or grow accordingly.",
   "start": 55.047,
   "end": 57.779
  },
  {
   "text": "For those of you who deal with compliance,",
   "start": 57.779,
   "end": 59.574
  },
  {
   "text": "you've probably noticed a big issue with your LLM providers.",
   "start": 59.574,
   "end": 63.16
  },
  {
   "text": "That is, even when you set the temperature",
   "start": 63.16,
   "end": 64.664
  },
  {
   "text": "to zero, these providers will send back",
   "start": 64.664,
   "end": 66.545
  },
  {
   "text": "different answers just because of all",
   "start": 66.545,
   "end": 68.186
  },
  {
   "text": "the different machines they use for computation.",
   "start": 68.186,
   "end": 70.203
  },
  {
   "text": "We hash every single machine that we use",
   "start": 70.203,
   "end": 72.339
  },
  {
   "text": "and we attach these hashes",
   "start": 72.339,
   "end": 73.416
  },
  {
   "text": "to every single response we give back.",
   "start": 73.416,
   "end": 75.532
  },
  {
   "text": "That way, anyone can reproduce our model returns",
   "start": 75.532,
   "end": 77.874
  },
  {
   "text": "with a byte-identical return, which is made",
   "start": 77.874,
   "end": 80.164
  },
  {
   "text": "even easier using our replay functionality.",
   "start": 80.164,
   "end": 82.549
  },
  {
   "text": "For those of you who have incredibly",
   "start": 82.549,
   "end": 84.062
  },
  {
   "text": "long sequentially chained workflows,",
   "start": 84.062,
   "end": 85.891
  },
  {
   "text": "we can run those independent steps in parallel",
   "start": 85.891,
   "end": 87.754
  },
  {
   "text": "using speculative tool predictions.",
   "start": 87.754,
   "end": 89.685
  },
  {
   "text": "That's part of what allows us",
   "start": 89.685,
   "end": 90.762
  },
  {
   "text": "to lower latency by up to 500 times.",
   "start": 90.762,
   "end": 93.355
  },
  {
   "text": "Finally, you can always manage your own",
   "start": 93.355,
   "end": 94.894
  },
  {
   "text": "data and your own model training.",
   "start": 94.894,
   "end": 96.479
  },
  {
   "text": "If we go to scores here, we can see exactly how",
   "start": 96.479,
   "end": 98.582
  },
  {
   "text": "different data points have been categorized,",
   "start": 98.582,
   "end": 100.377
  },
  {
   "text": "how they performed, what their costs were,",
   "start": 100.377,
   "end": 102.052
  },
  {
   "text": "and what their latency was. Then you can decide",
   "start": 102.052,
   "end": 104.069
  },
  {
   "text": "at each node whether to use our stand-ins or not.",
   "start": 104.069,
   "end": 106.513
  },
  {
   "text": "For those of you dealing with data",
   "start": 106.513,
   "end": 107.778
  },
  {
   "text": "handling policies, Dreaming is available",
   "start": 107.778,
   "end": 109.556
  },
  {
   "text": "in self-hosted and fully managed flavors.",
   "start": 109.556,
   "end": 111.898
  },
  {
   "text": "Keep on dreaming.",
   "start": 111.898,
   "end": 113.101
  }
 ],
